hs  which i think is something to keep a  close eye on because that  that threshold is kind of the the high  net worth individuals in my opinion  and then you have the thousand btc uh up  which is what what glass node likes to  just label as whales  and that's actually peaked out um and i  think coindesk put an article  out about this um and saying that it was  kind of a negative thing i just see it  as  kind of neutral because you started to  see these whales trim out of their  positions  um midway through each cycle and in 2017  they actually  the the peak of whales that were coming  on the network  was around 675 dollars which of course  was  you know very very far from the top  and it's just something that you start  to see them begin to take profits about  midway through the cycle  so that's not anything abnormal but it's  something i'm keeping an eye on just the  behavior of these different  uh entities because obviously um you  know the larger  the larger entities tend to be  institutions or  uh high net worth individuals and you  can get some signal based off of what  they're doing  um but i think that that 100 btc  to 1000 btc cohort is an interesting one  to keep an eye on  because although we just mentioned the  whales are selling off  that cohort is actually offsetting the  um  the decrease in supply coming from the  larger cohort  so it they're offsetting it by i think  it's 86 000.  um so what that illustrates to me is  either you know there's just more buying  from these high net worth individuals  or also maybe you know some of these the  larger cohorts let's say they have  um you know 10 000 btc in an address  right and bitcoin's gone up so much and  they want to say okay  i'm gonna de-risk um my holdings so i'm  gonna spread  um you know 1 000 into 10 different  wallets  and and that would move them into the  other threshold into that lower cohort  and then also if someone's right on the  verge like let's say they have a  thousand  two btc or a tho